From 3e6845b02b77ab21843413ba424b7cdb890642d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:17:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/56] drm/gma500: move the SGX545 driver into sgxfive/ behind
 a host interface

The GPU code reached into gma500's private data for register access, the
MMU and its own lifetime. Move it into drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/sgxfive/ and
give it a small interface (sgxfive.h): the host describes the DRM device, the
register block and the page directory it keeps in BIF directory list 0, and
forwards the SGX interrupt; sgxfive touches nothing else. gma_sgx.c is
gma500's side. This is the shape of the auxiliary-bus split the driver is
meant to take before it goes upstream. No functional change: every hardware
check passes on the GMA3600.

Assisted-by: LLM
